  <language>fr_FR</language>
  <keyword>netcdf.getConstant</keyword>
  <short_description>Retourne la valeur numerique d'une constante netCDF.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>value = netcdf.getConstant(name)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>arguments</param_name>
      <param_description>Input arguments follow the syntax shown above. File and group identifiers are numeric values returned by netCDF open, create, group, dimension, and variable definition calls. Named netCDF constants can be obtained with netcdf.getConstant.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>value</param_name>
      <param_description>Valeur retournee par l'operation netCDF.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>netcdf.getConstant expose une operation bas niveau de la bibliotheque netCDF.</p>
    <p>Ces fonctions utilisent des identifiants numeriques et suivent les conventions netCDF, notamment pour les indices, les modes et les constantes.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Exemple copiable pour netcdf.getConstant.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[mode = netcdf.getConstant('NC_CLOBBER')]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
